,{"node":"Ammonia burner","deviation":"High gauze temperature","cause":"High NH3 ratio, low gas flow","consequence":"Platinum loss, gauze damage, higher N2O","safeguard":"Gauze thermocouples, ratio control"},{"node":"NOx compressor","deviation":"Ammonium nitrate deposits","cause":"NH3 slip into the cooled gas","consequence":"Explosive AN salts in compressor and coolers","safeguard":"NH3 slip monitoring, washing routine"},{"node":"Absorber","deviation":"Loss of cooling","cause":"Cooling water pump trip","consequence":"High NOx emission, brown plume","safeguard":"NOx analyser, plant trip, spare pumps"},{"node":"Acid tank","deviation":"Loss of containment","cause":"Corrosion, overfill","consequence":"Corrosive acid spill, NOx fumes","safeguard":"Stainless tanks, bunds, level alarms"}],"process_hazards":[{"hazard":"Pressure","detail":"Up to 13 bar. Relief valves sized for fire and blocked outlet."},{"hazard":"High temperature","detail":"Up to 859 C. Creep, hydrogen attack and burns; refractory and tube skin temperature monitoring."},{"hazard":"Flammable materials","detail":"Ammonia. Hazardous area classification, ignition source control, gas detection, fire protection."},{"hazard":"Toxic materials","detail":"Ammonia, Nitric oxide, Nitrogen dioxide, Nitric acid. Toxic gas detection, emergency shutdown and isolation, escape sets, minimise inventory."},{"hazard":"Corrosive materials","detail":"Ammonia, Nitric oxide, Nitrogen dioxide, Nitric acid. Material selection, PPE, safety showers, bunded storage."}],"validation":[{"metric":"Ammonia consumption","model":281.913534,"published":282.0,"unit":"kg/t","error_pct":-0.030662,"inside_range":null,"source":"Uhde nitric acid brochure (2012), dual pressure","url":"https://pdfcoffee.com/uhde-nitric-acid-process-brochure-pdf-free.html","note":"","kind":"process","tolerance_pct":3,"pass":true},{"metric":"HP steam export","model":0.474163,"published":0.65,"unit":"t/t","error_pct":-27.051805,"inside_range":null,"source":"Uhde nitric acid brochure (2012), dual pressure, 40 bar 450 C","url":"https://pdfcoffee.com/uhde-nitric-acid-process-brochure-pdf-free.html","note":"","kind":"energy","tolerance_pct":30,"pass":true},{"metric":"Gauze temperature","model":858.889807,"published":[850,900],"unit":"C","error_pct":0.0,"inside_range":true,"source":"Fertilizers Europe Booklet 2, 1.7 to 6.5 bar band","url":"https://www.fertilizerseurope.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/Booklet_2_final.pdf","note":"","kind":"thermo","tolerance_pct":0,"pass":true},{"metric":"Tail gas flow","model":3214.483503,"published":[3100,3400],"unit":"Nm3/t","error_pct":0.0,"inside_range":true,"source":"Fertilizers Europe Booklet 2, section 4.1.1.1","url":"https://www.fertilizerseurope.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/Booklet_2_final.pdf","note":"","kind":"process","tolerance_pct":0,"pass":true},{"metric":"N2O in absorber tail gas (before abatement)","model":1108.988922,"published":[300,3500],"unit":"ppmv","error_pct":0.0,"inside_range":true,"source":"Fertilizers Europe Booklet 2, section 4.1.1.1","url":"https://www.fertilizerseurope.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/Booklet_2_final.pdf","note":"","kind":"process","tolerance_pct":0,"pass":true},{"metric":"N2O emission factor","model":2.5,"published":2.5,"unit":"kg/t","error_pct":0.0,"inside_range":null,"source":"IPCC 2006 Vol 3 Table 3.3, tail gas N2O destruction","url":"https://www.ipcc-nggip.iges.or.jp/public/2006gl/pdf/3_Volume3/V3_3_Ch3_Chemical_Industry.pdf","note":"Design input: abated emission set to this factor, shown for reference.","kind":"emissions","tolerance_pct":10,"pass":true}],"assumptions":["NO yield 96% from Fertilizers Europe Booklet 2 for 1.7 to 6.5 bar. N2O generation is the IPCC 2006 default for medium pressure plants (7 kg/t); the rest of the ammonia goes to N2.","With tertiary abatement the N2O leaving is the IPCC default for plants with tail gas N2O destruction (2.5 kg/t).","Gauze temperature solved as the adiabatic temperature of 10.5% NH3 in air (typical 9.5 to 11.